@intransigent
title: The <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> are as intransigent as ever.

We file it. There is nothing in it that changes what we are going to do this month, or next, and a party that has spent nine years explaining why we are the principal enemy is not going to be argued out of it by a document we were not supposed to read.

The memo goes into the drawer with the others.

@see_the_light
title: If only they could see the light.
on-arrival: left_strength += 2; reformist_strength -= 2 if reformist_strength >= 2

We say nothing publicly, because there is nothing useful to say publicly. But the memo circulates in our own building rather more widely than it strictly needs to, and the passage about the objections gets read aloud more than once.

It settles nothing. It shifts a little weight, though, in the argument our own factions have been having since the split: our <span style="color: #c00000;">Left</span> take it as evidence that there are people over there worth talking to, and our reformists take it as evidence of nothing at all, which is a slightly weaker position than the one they held last week.
